          "name": "fetch_feed",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:63490f79942a5b0a240b3bb9e7fe6cc6edd9d42498b1320626bb987a6030bc20",
          "description": "Fetch and parse an RSS or Atom feed. Returns feed metadata (title, subtitle, language) and the first `limit` entries in the order the feed lists them (title, link, published date, author, summary, tags). Entries are not re-sorted: most feeds list newest first, but that is not guaranteed. Use `limit` to cap how many entries you get back — feeds can be huge. Works with any publicly-accessible feed URL.",
